        "id": 202817,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-12T04:37:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>jffdougan wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>Jeysie wrote:<br>\n<blockquote>Finding out in the State of GTG video that the Kim Howell in Be the Gate is called \"Cursor\" was pretty amusing. \n</blockquote>\n<p>Did we get names for all of them?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>No, just her, sadly, as part of what IIRC was a discussion about puns and pun-using characters. (The pun IIRC being that a cursor is essentially a light-based arrow.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’m guessing she’s also the most foul-mouthed Sentinel Comics character.</p>",
